I don't think the myths specify how much Mjollnir weighs. I'm sure the
Eddas don't, but it may be mentioned somewhere else.
Also, there's a story about the hammer being stolen, so it can't be
that heavy.

Neutral weapons might be taken from Saberhagen's "Book of Swords"
series. Some of those swords are quite obviously *way* to powerful to
be used in a game (Shieldbreaker and Mindsword, for example) but the
more discreet ones might serve.
Coinspinner could act like a blessed luckstone (or affect luck in some
other way. Perhaps just prevent it from going negative) and
Sightblinder could give Invisibility and See Invisible.


